WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.420
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.460
Thinking about Buddhism as a religious tradition

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:15.870
requires us to keep in mind its deep roots as well as its wide branches.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.340
The roots of Buddhism stretch back in time

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:23.530
to about the fifth century BCE in a time of great social, economic,

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.810
and political change Buddhism's beginnings were profoundly

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.440
shaped by these conditions of changed in ancient India,

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.780
but Buddhism also represents a distinctive and innovative response

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.440
to these same conditions.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:43.180
While Buddhism has its historical roots in India reverence for the Buddha--

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.680
Buddhist thought and practice, and Buddhist institutions--

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.690
spread first throughout Asia and then across the entire world.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.150
Thus to understand Buddhism as a religion we always

00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:01.780
have to consider its deep roots in time, as well as its wide branches in space.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.450
Buddhists see the origins of their religious traditions

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.250
in the life of a prince named Siddhartha Gautama.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.900
Buddhist accounts of his life portray him

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.880
as leaving behind his royal status, his family, as well as his palace,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.460
to set out to find answers to deep questions about suffering

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:23.530
and its causes as well as to find out whether freedom

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.232
from suffering and death is possible.

00:01:26.232 --> 00:01:30.990
After years of searching and effort he discovered what he was seeking

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:37.140
and this discovery is encapsulated in the epithet, Buddha, the awakened one.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.570
The name Buddha-- a name that no parent ever gave--

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:46.390
indicates that the Buddha is to us as we are to people who are asleep.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:50.110
The name is a celebration of his achievement.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.390
On the basis of what he discovered the Buddha began

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:57.492
to teach the Dharma, truth with a capital T.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:02:01.310
And the diversity of Buddhist thought, over the ages across Asia,

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:04.200
represents the efforts of countless men and women

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.910
to understand and realize this truth and especially

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.820
to understand and realize what the Buddha taught us

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:14.970
about reality and human flourishing.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.890
The Buddha not only taught ideas, but also a way of life.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:22.710
The Buddha established institutions that grounded the community that

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:27.370
developed around him and teachings that provided guidance to that community

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:33.390
on how to live, so that its members could achieve enlightenment themselves.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:37.702
Those who set out to live as the Buddha taught are called the Sangha.

00:02:37.702 --> 00:02:39.740
From the beginning the Buddha's disciples

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:45.330
included both female and male monastics as well as male and female laypeople.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.470
This way of life and these institutions were enduring

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:53.130
but they also proved to be very adaptable to new settings

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:54.130
and circumstances.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:59.180
As early as the first century the tradition began to travel over the Silk

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:04.370
Road into West and Central Asia, and by the eighth century Buddhism was well

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.300
established in China, Korea, .

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:11.910
And Japan Buddhism also spread south across India to Sri Lanka,

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:16.410
and to Southeast Asia from Burma to Vietnam and Java.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:20.520
This spread of Buddhism across Asia enriched the Buddhist heritage

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.710
by the addition of new texts into the canons of Buddhist scriptures

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:27.610
and in this regard Buddhists have had more open canons

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.600
than have Christians and Muslims.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.930
In time some Buddhist communities also developed

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.280
dual canons in which one portion of scripture

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.020
was interpreted in the light of the subsequent canon of scriptures that

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.980
was deemed to be closer to the intentions of the Buddha

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:48.070
as a teacher Buddhist's dual canons are analogous to the combination

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:51.350
of the Old Testament and the New Testament in the Christian Bible,

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:55.770
or the Quran-- in relation to the texts of other peoples of the book.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:59.140
The Buddhist heritage was also greatly enriched

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.810
by the translation of Buddhist scriptures

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:06.260
into many different languages, including Pali and Sanskrit in South

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:11.700
and Southeast Asia, to Tibetan and Chinese in Central and East Asia.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:14.860
The translation of Buddhist scriptures into different languages

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:19.529
was always an enormous project since the canonical collections

00:04:19.529 --> 00:04:22.400
of texts that carry the Buddha's teachings can

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.950
include thousands of individual texts.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:29.400
The complexity and diversity of Buddhist thought and practice--

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.500
the richness of its character in local settings--

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.390
are so pronounced that when Europeans first encountered Buddhists

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.930
in their explorations at the beginning of the colonial,

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.520
age it took them quite a while to realize

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.890
that the religion they encountered in Sri Lanka

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:47.180
was historically related to what they saw in Japan.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.710
And yet amidst all the diversity and complexity

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:54.590
of ideas, practices, experiences, values, and institutions,

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:59.290
we can see that Buddhists still have much in common and that they share,

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:03.740
especially, a sustained attentiveness to suffering and the stopping

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.022
of suffering.

00:05:05.022 --> 00:05:07.770
Just as the Buddha said about his long career of teaching,

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:12.580
"Both formally, and now, it is only suffering and the stopping

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.020
of suffering that I describe."

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.570
[MUSIC PLAYING]

